course: dictionary
lesson: 10294
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Touch is a short word with several meanings. The words around it tell you which meaning you need. «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone.» Here touch means putting your hand or body on something.
explain: «Her letter touched me.» Touch does not mean using a hand here, because a letter cannot put a finger on you. Look at the rest of the sentence: touched means the letter made her feel something, probably a kind or sad feeling.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Keep in touch» means stay in contact, and «a touch of salt» means a small amount. If the swapped meaning does not make sense, try another meaning.
fact: Touch can be a verb (I touch, she touches, they touched) or a noun (a touch, the sense of touch).
fact: Your sense of touch uses nerves in your skin to feel pressure, heat, cold and pain.
fact: «Never touch a bat»: some bats carry viruses, so keep your hands off wild animals.
fact: Safety rules: don't touch hot things, sharp things, or plugs with wet hands.
fact: Your body belongs to you. No one should touch your private parts. If anyone does, say no and tell a grown-up you trust.
exercise: «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone.» In this sentence, what does touch mean? | To make someone feel sad | A small amount | *To put your hand or body on something | To stay in contact with someone
exercise: «Her letter touched me.» What does touched mean here? | It put a hand on me | *It made me feel a kind or sad feeling | It was heavy and rough | It was a small amount of paper
exercise: «Most spiders have eight eyes, but many see poorly and rely on touch and vibration.» Many spiders depend on which sense when they cannot see well? | Taste | Sight | *Touch | Hearing
test: «Never touch a bat; some bats carry rabies or similar viruses.» Why should you not touch a bat? | Bats are always friendly | Bats are too big to hold | *Some bats carry viruses that can make you ill | Bats are too slow to catch
test: What does «a touch of salt» mean? | A large amount of salt | *A small amount of salt | Salt you must never eat | A very hot dish
exam: «The hairs of some caterpillars, such as the oak processionary, cause rashes, so you do not touch hairy caterpillars.» Why do you not touch hairy caterpillars? | They taste bitter | They are too quick to catch | They are too big to hold | *Their hairs can cause rashes on your skin
